{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Hello,</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This VR game is a time machine. You don't get to choose where you go. When you pull the lever you are taken somewhere random.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You receive a date telling you where you are in time and the doors open. There's no way of predicting where you'll end up. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can't leave the time machine -  you can stick your head out, but be warned sometimes you might not want to. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Where Will I Go?</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You might end up somewhere significant or you might end up somewhere totally ordinary.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you don't like where you are then you pull the lever again. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Controls</strong> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game takes place in a single 2x3m room. You can use teleport and smooth locomotion to move around in the space if you would like to play sitting down. Its best played roomscale. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Have fun! </p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2707810?t=1758760941","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/0054aac222e4321571682356ab6b0a98cc7400da/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1758760941","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/8cfa3ee123239fd3fd3d2f69748204a284516486/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1758760941","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/8cfa3ee123239fd3fd3d2f69748204a284516486/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1758760941","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Tracked Controller Support","id":52},{"description":"VR Only","id":54},{"description":"Camera Comfort","id":67},{"description":"Playable without Timed Input","id":74},{"description":"Stereo Sound","id":69},{"description":"Surround Sound","id":70},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[5],"notes":"The Time Machine presents dioramas of real historical settings. There is no gore, violence, or graphic content, but some locations may depict politically or socially contentious moments in history."},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Hello,</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This VR game is a time machine. You don't get to choose where you go. When you pull the lever you are taken somewhere random.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You receive a date telling you where you are in time and the doors open. There's no way of predicting where you'll end up. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can't leave the time machine -  you can stick your head out, but be warned sometimes you might not want to. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Where Will I Go?</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You might end up somewhere significant or you might end up somewhere totally ordinary.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you don't like where you are then you pull the lever again. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Controls</strong> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game takes place in a single 2x3m room. You can use teleport and smooth locomotion to move around in the space if you would like to play sitting down. Its best played roomscale. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Have fun! </p>","developers":["Lionel Marsden"],"genres":[{"description":"Adventure","id":"25"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/9980959586ccb21c394c6c209a65b04451105a1f/header.jpg?t=1758760941","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":[],"movies":[{"dash_av1":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/2707810/860464626/b27528184dc941a199df1490317ebe451ac334df/1751116142/dash_av1.mpd?t=1751117812","dash_h264":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/2707810/860464626/b27528184dc941a199df1490317ebe451ac334df/1751116142/dash_h264.mpd?t=1751117812","highlight":true,"hls_h264":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/2707810/860464626/b27528184dc941a199df1490317ebe451ac334df/1751116142/hls_264_master.m3u8?t=1751117812","id":256993405,"mp4":{"480":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/256993405/movie480.mp4?t=1751117812","max":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/256993405/movie_max.mp4?t=1751117812"},"name":"Teaser","thumbnail":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/256993405/08d07222dcc2cc41ea37ad60d857a4548011e362/movie_600x337.jpg?t=1751117812","webm":{"480":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/256993405/movie480_vp9.webm?t=1751117812","max":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/256993405/movie_max_vp9.webm?t=1751117812"}}],"name":"The Time Machine","package_groups":[],"pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Core i5-7500 / Ryzen 5 1600<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 12 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> GTX 1060 / RX 580 - 6GB VRAM<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Versio